{
  "name": "aud_audio",
  "summary": "The Audanika Audio Engine: AudEngine plays a graph of aud_audio_graph through an output stream of aud_audio_io, registers the node types of DSP packages and keeps the lifecycle; one API on native platforms and the web, iOS and Android first, macOS with the Mac app (release-005).",
  "domain": [
    "The Audanika Audio Engine",
    "The sample cache budget of the process and the numbers of the engine: render time, xruns, command to sound, cache and loads",
    "Engine extensions that live with the engine and close before its graph, and the engine's timing for the control side (ticket 26)",
    "The load governor (ticket 29): AudLoadGovernor sets an AudLoadBudget - e.g. the voice budget of the sampler nodes - from the mean render share, the xruns and the units in use; AudLoadPolicy without timers for simulations; AudDeviceClass reads the device's model, cores, clocks and media performance class for the start budget",
    "The example app in the pub workspace: oscillator page, SFZ sampler page with a keyboard, integration tests that measure the M1 budgets"
  ],
  "interfaces": {
    "uses": {
      "aud_audio_core": "ABI version, results, clock and value types",
      "aud_audio_graph": "the graph the engine renders, aud_graph_render",
      "aud_audio_io": "the session and the output stream",
      "aud_audio_web": "the web build, a stub until S5",
      "aud_dsp_sampler": "the example app plays the sampler"
    },
    "usedBy": {
      "aud_audio_ui_graph_edit": "consumes this package",
      "aud_audio_ui_controls": "consumes this package",
      "aud_audio_ui_keyboard": "consumes this package",
      "aud_audio_ui_waveform": "consumes this package",
      "aud_audio_bench": "consumes this package",
      "aud_audio_midi": "the engine its MIDI bridge extends, its timing and node packages"
    }
  }
}
